<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali Tegin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1034</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali Tegin was a prince of the Kara-Khanid dynasty who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> from about 1020 until his death in 1034. He fought rival members of his family and the Ghaznavids, and in 1025 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> joined the eastern khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-qadir-khan">Yusuf Qadir Khan</a> against him, driving him out for a time. He used Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> bands as allies, helping the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> in the region.</p></div>
